.TH COSMIC-EXT-IME 1 "September 2026" "cosmic-ext-ime 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
cosmic-ext-ime \- Cangjie, Quick and RIME input method for the COSMIC desktop
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B cosmic-ext-ime
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B cosmic-ext-ime
is a native Wayland input method (zwp_input_method_v2) for COSMIC. It provides
Cangjie and Quick (倉頡／速成) through libcangjie2, or any RIME schema through
librime, with a candidate popup that follows the COSMIC theme.
.PP
It is started automatically with the COSMIC session. Only one input method may
be active on a seat: stop IBus or Fcitx5 first, and make sure GTK_IM_MODULE,
QT_IM_MODULE and XMODIFIERS are not set, so toolkits use Wayland text-input.
.PP
Chinese input is enabled while a Chinese keyboard layout is active in COSMIC
Settings > Keyboard > Input Sources; switch with Super+Space.
.SH CONFIGURATION
Settings are stored via cosmic-config in
.I ~/.config/cosmic/io.github.wanleung.CosmicExtIme/v1/
and applied live. Use
.BR cosmic-ext-ime-settings (1)
to change them. RIME user data lives in
.IR ~/.local/share/cosmic-ext-ime/rime/ .
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B RUST_LOG
Log level filter, e.g. RUST_LOG=debug.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR cosmic-ext-ime-settings (1)
.SH AUTHOR
Wan Leung Wong
